{
 "about": {
  "traffic": "each agents trace's proxy_calls in order (desk-hand, desk-hand-go, desk-langgraph, desk-sdk, patterns, patterns-go; repeats kept), then the judge set's recordings in file order: 957 calls, one at a time, with x-team (desk, patterns, judge) and x-request-tag (the ticket id in the messages, or none)",
  "latency": "P6: p50_ms and p95_ms are nearest-rank percentiles over each call's recorded wall clock (upstream.ms in agents/data/recordings), joined by the driver; a trace's ms is the gateway's own clock (about a millisecond in replay) and is not used for them",
  "time": "replay time: the gateway's clock starts at 0 and moves by each call's recorded ms and any limiter wait, so the limiter and the cache ttl see the recorded pace; nothing sleeps",
  "cost": "cost_usd is the gateway's ledger: the recorded usage priced with the LLMs lab's table; a cache hit books $0; prompt_cache_* are the recorded prompt-cache tokens of the calls that reached the upstream",
  "cache": "all 20 hits are cross-set repeats of a tool-free end_turn call an earlier set made first (19 in patterns-go from patterns, 1 in desk-hand-go from desk-hand); the 6 within-set pattern repeats carry tools, so the cache skips them",
  "counts": "retries: traces with more than one upstream attempt; refusals: status 400, 402, 404 or 429",
  "all": "the figures over every call; sets and teams split them",
  "cases": "infra/data/fixtures/cases.json through stages.run_cases: each case's decisions and status",
  "injector": "one request through the gateway against injector.make_server on each script in infra/data/fixtures/injector, retry.base_ms 1, rng Random(0): its status, outcome, decisions and attempts (model, status, backoff_ms)",
  "gate": "replay.py --gate: ledger (per desk set, the gateway's ledger plus what its cache hits were recorded at equals the agents traces' cost within 1e-9; the independent check), budgets, stages (a failed or errored trace fails it), figures (the hit rate and p95 rebuilt from the same run's traces and recordings: a consistency check, not an independent one; drift from the committed capstone.json is --check's job)"
 },
